#!RuleTest
#test DRAFT-900043 expect=violation domain=DS
#note "RE-POINTED skipped -> violation 2026-08-27 (owner ruling, evidence in REMOVE-34-EVIDENCE.md): DSSCAT was removed from Requirements.Variables.All because it is Permissible in this domain and NO rule anywhere reports its absence -- not a specific presence rule, and not the generic Required/Expected rules, which do not cover Permissible variables. Leaving the All entry silenced the defect with nothing else reporting it. SUPERSEDES this fixture's earlier rationale ('skips the rule rather than flagging every DSCAT row'): that argued the flood case, but DSCAT == "DISPOSITION EVENT" still restricts the rows, so an absent DSSCAT yields a SUBSET, not every row -- and subset means unguarded under M2-D24 / the absent-column bucket classifier. The rule now reports 2 violation(s) here."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
#expectViolationCount 2
dataset DS class=EVENTS label="Disposition"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col DSSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col DSCAT    type=Char label="Category for Disposition Event"
col EPOCH    type=Char label="Epoch"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | DS | 01-701-1015 | 1 | DISPOSITION EVENT | TREATMENT
CDISCPILOT01 | DS | 01-701-1015 | 2 | DISPOSITION EVENT | TREATMENT
